Files taken from Headroom, with their upstream paths
----------------------------------------------------

  masks.py                     headroom/compression/masks.py
  handlers/base.py             headroom/compression/handlers/base.py
  handlers/json_handler.py     headroom/compression/handlers/json_handler.py
  handlers/code_handler.py     headroom/compression/handlers/code_handler.py
  segmenter.py                 headroom/transforms/mixed_content.py
  lossless.py                  headroom/transforms/lossless_compaction.py

Statement of changes (Apache-2.0 section 4b)
--------------------------------------------

  * Absolute ``headroom.*`` imports were rewritten as relative imports, so the
    folder can be vendored under any name.
  * detector.py replaces Headroom's Magika-based ML detection with rules; it is
    original to this package, not a port.
  * reducers.py replaces Kompress, Headroom's learned span compressor, with
    deterministic rules; also original to this package.
  * segmenter.py drops the tag-protection placeholder isolation, which depends
    on Headroom's Rust extension, and types log lines ahead of search results.
  * handlers/text_handlers.py, handlers/mixed_handler.py and
    handlers/data_handlers.py are original to this package.
  * lossless.py is unchanged apart from its module docstring.
  * The CCR retrieval store was removed; CompressionResult.original carries the
    input instead.

Not included
------------

Headroom's log, diff, search and text compressors are implemented in Rust
(``headroom._core``) and cannot be vendored as a source folder. The handlers
here are independent rule-based implementations.
